source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira passes `&#92;`, the character reference for a backslash, through into the cell text. jiro keeps it as the cell's text, and writes one where a cell value would otherwise end in a raw backslash.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|a&#92;|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a&#92;</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
| h |
| --- |
| a&#92; |
-- warnings.json --
[]
